Make the bundled BLT 2.4j subset (bgexec, busy, drag&drop) work with
Tcl/Tk 8.6 on 64-bit systems.

- bltWindow.c: include Tk's real tkInt.h instead of private copies of
  the Tk 8.0-8.4 TkDisplay/TkWindow layouts, which no longer match.
- bltInt.h: only declare the namespace API for Tcl < 8.5 (it is public
  since then, with different prototypes); guard TkpClipMask.
- Route BLT's malloc/free/strdup/calloc through Tcl's allocator, as
  BLT already did on Windows: memory from Tcl_SplitList & co. was
  released with libc free(), aborting with "free(): invalid size".
- Tcl_GetChannelHandle stores a pointer-sized handle: don't let it
  write into an int (broke "2>@stderr" redirection, e.g. Disk Usage).
- Tcl_DetachPids takes an array of pointer-sized Tcl_Pid, not ints.
- Accept any Tk 8.6.x instead of requiring exactly "8.6".
- tkAppInit.c: load [incr Tcl] 4 with package require instead of
  linking libitcl from its private directory.

